  "handoff": {
    "summary": "Implemented a deterministic release artifact manifest creator and fail-closed verifier. The manifest separates reproducible artifact/source/target/capability identity from optional SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH creation provenance, streams SHA-256 checksums, records normalized Node/compiler/native-math build identity, and supports exact Git or explicit source-archive provenance. Nine focused tests cover stable output, multiple artifacts, normalized toolchain paths, artifact and manifest tampering, non-regular substitutions, malformed and noncanonical input, dirty Git sources, source archives, and the CLI.",
    "risks": [
      "pnpm test:portable reaches the expected shared integration boundary: test/test-manifest.test.cjs rejects the new test until test/release-manifest.cjs is registered in test/node-test-manifest.cjs. All preceding portable tests passed once deferred FLINT, M4RI, FFLAS, and graph adapters were provisioned."
    ],
    "next_steps": [
      "In the integration lane, add test/release-manifest.cjs to the unit array in test/node-test-manifest.cjs, then rerun pnpm test:portable.",
      "Wire the manifest creator into the release artifact assembly lane and supply its authoritative capability report; signing and notarization can later cover the canonical manifest and artifact set."
    ]
  }
